['Here is a basic implementation of `StateLoader` class in Java. This example uses LRU (Least Recently Used) cache to manage bitmaps. 

```java
import java.io.*;
import java.util.*;
import android.graphics.Bitmap;
import android.graphics.BitmapFactory;

public class StateLoader {
    private static final String DEFAULT_THEME_PATH = "/path/to/default/theme";
    private static final int MAX_CACHE_SIZE = 100; // Adjust this value according to your needs

    private LRUCache<String, Bitmap> cache;
    private File defaultThemeDir;

    public StateLoader() {
        cache = new LRUCache<>(MAX_CACHE_SIZE);

        String themePath = System.getProperty("theme.path"); // Get the path from system properties
        if (themePath == null) {
            defaultThemeDir = new File(DEFAULT_THEME_PATH);
        } else {
            defaultThemeDir = new File(themePath);
        }
    }

    public Bitmap loadBitmap(String fileName) throws IOException {
        Bitmap bitmap = cache.get(fileName);

        if (bitmap == null) {
            File imageFile = new File(defaultThemeDir, fileName);

            try (InputStream in = new BufferedInputStream(new FileInputStream(imageFile))) {
                bitmap = BitmapFactory.decodeStream(in);

                // Add the bitmap to cache
                if (bitmap != null) {
                    cache.put(fileName, bitmap);
                }
            } catch (IOException e) {
                throw new IOException("Failed to load image file: " + fileName, e);
            }
        }

        return bitmap;
    }

    public Object loadStateObject(String fileName) throws IOException, ClassNotFoundException {
        File stateFile = new File(defaultThemeDir, fileName);

        try (ObjectInputStream in = new ObjectInputStream(new BufferedInputStream(new FileInputStream(stateFile)))) {
            return in.readObject();
        } catch (IOException e) {
            throw new IOException("Failed to load state object from file: " + fileName, e);
        }
    }

    private static class LRUCache<K, V> extends LinkedHashMap<K, V> {
        private int maxSize;

        public LRUCache(int maxSize) {
            super(maxSize * 4 / 3, 0.75f, true); // Load factor and ordering mode are not important here
            this.maxSize = maxSize;
        }

        @Override
        protected boolean removeEldestEntry(Map.Entry<K, V> eldest) {
            return size() > maxSize;
        }
    }
}
```
This code assumes that the system property `theme.path` is set to the path of the theme directory if it exists. If not, it falls back to a default path specified by `DEFAULT_THEME_PATH`. The bitmaps are loaded from files in this directory and cached for future use. 

The cache uses an LRU strategy: when the cache is full, the least recently used item (the one at the end of the linked list) is removed to make room for a new item. This ensures that frequently accessed items stay in memory while infrequently accessed ones are evicted.

Please note that this code does not handle all possible exceptions and edge cases. You may need to add more error handling and validation according to your specific requirements. Also, the caching mechanism is very basic and might not be suitable for all use cases. Depending on your application's needs, you might want to consider using a disk-based cache or a third-party library that provides more advanced caching features.
']

