["Here is an example of how you might implement this using C11's `_Atomic` types and POSIX threads (pthreads). This solution uses a simple linked list to store the contexts, with each node containing a pointer to a `UEContextInfo` structure. The list is protected by a mutex for thread safety.

```c
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <pthread.h>
#include <stdatomic.h>

typedef struct UEContextInfo {
    int ueId;
    int rnti;
    _Atomic(bool) crcIndication;
    time_t timestamp; // Add a timestamp field for context expiration
} UEContextInfo;

typedef struct Node {
    UEContextInfo *context;
    struct Node *next;
} Node;

Node *head = NULL;
pthread_mutex_t mutex = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;
atomic_int maxSize = 1000; // Maximum size of the context pool

void addContext(UEContextInfo *context) {
    pthread_mutex_lock(&mutex);

    if (listLength() >= atomic_load(&maxSize)) {
        resizePool(); // Resize the pool if it's full
    }

    Node *node = malloc(sizeof(Node));
    node->context = context;
    node->next = head;
    head = node;

    pthread_mutex_unlock(&mutex);
}

void removeContext(int ueId) {
    pthread_mutex_lock(&mutex);

    Node **ptr = &head;
    while (*ptr != NULL) {
        if ((*ptr)->context->ueId == ueId) {
            Node *temp = *ptr;
            *ptr = temp->next;
            free(temp->context);
            free(temp);
            break;
        }
        ptr = &(*ptr)->next;
    }

    pthread_mutex_unlock(&mutex);
}

void resizePool() {
    atomic_store(&maxSize, atomic_load(&maxSize) * 2); // Double the size of the pool
}

int listLength() {
    int length = 0;
    Node *node = head;

    while (node != NULL) {
        length++;
        node = node->next;
    }

    return length;
}

void evictExpiredContexts(time_t currentTime, time_t expirationPeriod) {
    pthread_mutex_lock(&mutex);

    Node **ptr = &head;
    while (*ptr != NULL) {
        if (currentTime - (*ptr)->context->timestamp > expirationPeriod) {
            Node *temp = *ptr;
            *ptr = temp->next;
            free(temp->context);
            free(temp);
        } else {
            ptr = &(*ptr)->next;
        }
    }

    pthread_mutex_unlock(&mutex);
}
```
This code provides a basic implementation of the context pool. It includes functions for adding and removing contexts, resizing the pool when it's full, and evicting expired contexts based on their timestamp field. The `maxSize` variable is used to limit the number of contexts in the pool, and can be adjusted as needed.
"]

