The `computeHash` method sanitizes the input by removing non-alphanumeric characters, logs the sanitized input, and then computes and returns the MD5 hash of the sanitized string.

Finally, this code uses Java's built-in logging framework to log any input sanitization activities for auditing purposes. This can be adjusted according to your needs.
