['Here is a basic implementation of such a function in PHP using Redis for caching and MySQL for database operations. This code does not include the payment gateway integration part as it would be quite complex to implement here. 

```php
<?php
class UserAuthService {
    private $redis;
    private $db;

    public function __construct() {
        $this->redis = new Redis();
        $this->redis->connect('127.0.0.1', 6379); // replace with your redis server details

        $this->db = new PDO('mysql:host=localhost;dbname=test', 'username', 'password'); // replace with your db credentials
    }

    public function authenticate($userId, $accessToken) {
        if ($this->redis->exists("user:$userId")) {
            $cachedAccessToken = $this->redis->get("user:$userId");
            if ($cachedAccessToken == $accessToken) {
                return true; // cache hit
            } else {
                $this->refreshUser($userId, $accessToken); // refresh access token in background
                return false; // cache miss but still valid
            }
        } else {
            $profile = $this->getProfileFromDB($userId);
            if ($profile['access_token'] == $accessToken) {
                $this->redis->set("user:$userId", $accessToken, 3600); // cache for an hour
                return true;
            } else {
                return false;
            }
        }
    }

    private function refreshUser($userId, $newAccessToken) {
        $this->redis->set("user:$userId", $newAccessToken, 3600); // cache for an hour

        // offload the DB operation to avoid blocking API calls
        go(function() use ($userId, $newAccessToken) {
            $this->db->exec("UPDATE users SET access_token = '$newAccessToken' WHERE id = $userId");
        });
    }

    private function getProfileFromDB($userId) {
        $stmt = $this->db->prepare('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?');
        $stmt->execute([$userId]); 

        return $stmt->fetch();
    }
}
?>
```
This code uses Redis for caching user profiles and access tokens, which reduces the load on the database. It also offloads the DB operation to refresh the access token in a non-blocking way, ensuring uninterrupted user experience. However, this is a simplified version of what you might need for a high-traffic e-commerce platform. For example, it doesn't include error handling or logging which would be necessary in a production environment.
']

