<?php
class UserService {
    private $recentPasswords = []; // Array to store recent passwords
    private $maxRetries = 5; // Maximum number of retries for service operations
    private $backoffBase = 1000000; // Base delay in microseconds for exponential backoff

    public function updatePassword($userId, $newPassword) {
        $this->validateNewPassword($newPassword);

        if (in_array($newPassword, array_slice($this->recentPasswords, -10))) { // Check uniqueness in recent passwords
            throw new Exception('The new password is not unique within the last 10 passwords.');
        }

        $retries = 0;
        $delay = $this->backoffBase;

        while ($retries < $this->maxRetries) {
            try {
                $response = // Call to your service here, e.g., using GuzzleHttp\Client

                if ($response->getStatusCode() === 200) {
                    $this->recentPasswords[] = $newPassword; // Add new password to recent passwords
                    return true;
                } else {
                    throw new Exception('Service operation failed.');
                }
            } catch (Exception $e) {
                $retries++;

                if ($retries >= $this->maxRetries) {
                    error_log("Circuit breaker tripped after $retries retries.");
                    throw new Exception('Maximum number of retries reached.');
                }

                usleep($delay); // Exponential backoff delay
                $delay *= 2;
            }
        }

        return false;
    }

    private function validateNewPassword($newPassword) {
        if (strlen($newPassword) < 8) {
            throw new Exception('The new password must be at least 8 characters long.');
        }

        // Add more validation criteria as needed, e.g., complexity check
    }
}
?>
```
This code uses a simple array to store recent passwords and checks uniqueness against them. It also implements an exponential backoff retry mechanism with a maximum number of retries. If the service operation fails after reaching the maximum number of retries, it trips the circuit breaker and throws an exception. 

