['Here's a basic implementation of what you asked for. This code assumes that you have an `IDataRepository` interface with methods for adding and retrieving data, as well as a `DataItem` class representing the custom data structure you want to deserialize from the binary file. 

```csharp
using System;
using System.IO;
using System.Runtime.Serialization.Formatters.Binary;
using System.Threading;

public interface IDataRepository
{
    void Add(object item);
    object Get();
}

public class DataItem { }

public class BinaryFileLoader
{
    private readonly ILogger _logger;
    private readonly IDataRepository _repository;
    private readonly ReaderWriterLockSlim _lock = new ReaderWriterLockSlim();

    public BinaryFileLoader(ILogger logger, IDataRepository repository)
    {
        _logger = logger;
        _repository = repository;
    }

    public void LoadFromBinaryFile(string filePath)
    {
        try
        {
            using (var stream = new FileStream(filePath, FileMode.Open))
            {
                var formatter = new BinaryFormatter();

                while (stream.Position < stream.Length)
                {
                    var dataItem = (DataItem)formatter.Deserialize(stream);

                    _lock.EnterWriteLock();
                    try
                    {
                        _repository.Add(dataItem);
                    }
                    finally
                    {
                        _lock.ExitWriteLock();
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            _logger.LogError("An error occurred while loading data from binary file", ex);
        }
    }
}
```
This code uses a `ReaderWriterLockSlim` to ensure thread safety when adding items to the repository, which is an efficient locking mechanism for scenarios where there are more readers than writers. It also logs any exceptions that occur during deserialization using an injected logger interface. 

Please note that this is a basic implementation and may need to be adjusted based on your specific requirements and constraints. For example, you might want to use a different data structure or repository for storing the deserialized items if performance becomes an issue with large files. Also, depending on your architecture, you might want to consider using other concurrency primitives like `SemaphoreSlim` or `Monitor` instead of `ReaderWriterLockSlim`.
']

