['Here is a basic implementation of an event stream parser in Java. This code does not include all the mentioned engineering challenges but it provides a good starting point for building a robust solution. 

```java
import java.io.*;
import java.util.*;
import java.time.*;

public class EventStreamParser {
    private static final String DELIMITER = ",";

    public List<Event> parseLogFile(String filePath) throws IOException {
        List<Event> eventList = new ArrayList<>();

        try (BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new FileReader(filePath))) {
            String line;

            while ((line = br.readLine()) != null) {
                Event event = parseLogLine(line);

                if (event != null) {
                    eventList.add(event);
                }
            }
        }

        return Collections.unmodifiableList(new ArrayList<>(eventList));
    }

    private Event parseLogLine(String line) {
        String[] logParts = line.split(DELIMITER);

        if (logParts.length < 3) {
            System.err.println("Malformed event: " + line);
            return null;
        }

        Instant timestamp = Instant.parse(logParts[0]);
        String type = logParts[1];
        Map<String, String> metadata = parseMetadata(Arrays.copyOfRange(logParts, 2, logParts.length));

        return new Event(timestamp, type, metadata);
    }

    private Map<String, String> parseMetadata(String[] metadataParts) {
        Map<String, String> metadata = new HashMap<>();

        for (String part : metadataParts) {
            String[] keyValuePair = part.split("=");

            if (keyValuePair.length == 2) {
                metadata.put(keyValuePair[0], keyValuePair[1]);
            } else {
                System.err.println("Malformed metadata: " + Arrays.toString(metadataParts));
            }
        }

        return metadata;
    }
}
```

This code reads the log file line by line, parses each line into an Event object and adds it to a list. If a line is malformed (i.e., does not contain enough parts), it prints an error message and skips that line. The same applies for metadata. 

